// Title: Sandbox / Virtualization Environment Detection
// Sigma ID: a1eceaaa-7b4b-52bc-565d-2b34ce72abc6
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Entroprism (Beijing Yijun Foreign Trade Co., Ltd.)
// Date: 2026-11-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: T1497
// Tags: detection.threat_hunting
// Description: Detects attempts to identify virtualization or sandbox environments via VM artifact queries or
//   macOS hardware model probing.
// False positives:
//   - legitimate virtualization management tools
// References:
//   - https://entroprism.net
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/02019c7f616fa2b4879138907ad45880092bf5b9/rules/windows/process_creation/sandbox__virtualization_environment_detection.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "VMware" or ProcessCommandLine contains "VBoxService" or ProcessCommandLine contains "vbox" or ProcessCommandLine contains "qemu-ga") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "sysctl hw.model" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ioreg -l")
